// Scoped lint waivers for our OWN continuant-coprocessor RTL.
//
// Policy: width / unsigned / truncation / latch findings are FIXED in the RTL,
// never waived (they can hide real bugs). This file waives only UNOPTFLAT, and
// only for the reason below.
//
// UNOPTFLAT on the combinational scan / gradient datapaths: these fold a 2x2
// transfer matrix (or a gradient) as a strictly feed-forward chain that passes
// stage k-1 -> stage k through an unpacked array. The scheduler analyses each
// array as a single node and, because the chain also threads through the
// HardFloat decode blocks, reports "circular combinational logic" on a signal
// deep inside HardFloat (e.g. recFNToFN d_p01.sign). It is NOT a real loop:
//   * different array ELEMENTS are read vs written each stage, and
//   * the Yosys synthesis dry-run (docs/SYNTHESIS_DRYRUN.md) maps every module
//     with no combinational-loop error -- independent confirmation.
// UNOPTFLAT does not affect simulation correctness (Verilator still settles the
// logic); it is a scheduling/optimization hint. split_var declines to split the
// arrays on this tool version, and the loop representative lands in third-party
// files, so a rule-level waiver is the clean option. Every other lint rule stays
// fatal for our RTL.
`verilator_config
lint_off -rule UNOPTFLAT
